 "notes": "E363 duplicates the unit's own row; its swimming pools are recorded once (own row, position none). Other E/S duplicates (E359, E360, E371, E349, E343, E344) recorded once. SWP: Beit Jubr et Tahtani matches Nigro N36 (250 m); its birkeh 'immediately south of the fort' takes grid N36. Kanat Musa: Birket Musa (named) given grid S2551; the cistern 'east of the Birket Musa' coded words E, relative to other; the other aqueduct cisterns (Ain el Aujah to Kh. el Mefjir, Bir Heider 8 miles) are not locatable within 2 km and not coded. Tell es Sultan entry: section 6 (Tellul Abu el 'Aleik = the unit) has only a 'rectangular chamber' (a room) and a bridge, not coded; it says the site 'is not otherwise provided with water' (supply, not a pool absence; not recorded as absence). Its Tell es Sultan/'Ain es Sultan features and Warren's mound No. 3 graves lie near 'Ain es Sultan (Tell es Sultan is not within 2 km); not coded. Clearly different places, ignored: Rujm el Mogheifir (Ps, 4.7 km), Hajr el Asbah, Khurbet Haiyan, Mugharet el Jai, Khan Hathrurah, Khurbet es Sumrah (6.8-12.7 km). Tell es Sultan and Mugharet el Jai texts are cut at 12,000 characters. N7 pits (2nd century AD) coded U. Rock shelters, niches, recesses, fissures not coded. No explicit absence statements."
}